==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|modifien|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|modifier|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|modificare||to limit, control, regulate, deponent|lang=la}}, from {{term|modificari||to measure off, set bound to, moderate}}, from {{term|modus||measure}} + {{term|facere||to make}}; see [[mode]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-modify.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|modif|i|ed}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[make]] partial [[change]]s to.
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To [[be]] or [[become]] modified.

====Synonyms====
* [[adapt]], [[alter]], [[amend]], [[revamp]], [[rework]]

====Related terms====
* [[modification]]
* [[modifier]]

